==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|spīwan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*spīwaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ptyēw-||to spit, vomit}}. Compare Dutch {{term|spuwen|lang=nl}}, {{term|spugen|lang=nl}}, English {{term|spew|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|spy|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃpaɪ̯ən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-speien.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|speit|spie|gespien|past participle 2=gespieen}}

# to [[spit]]
# {{context|euphemistic|lang=de}} to [[vomit]]

====Conjugation====
* The past participle currently has two different pronunciations: one corresponding to {{term|gespien}} and the other to {{term|gespieen}}. Today, though, the only official spelling is {{term||gespien}}, regardless of pronunciation.
* Similary the conjunctive (subjunctive) is spelled {{term|spiee}} or {{term|spie}}. Both are pronounced [ˈʃpiːə], but only the latter spelling is official nowadays.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|spit}} [[spucken]]
* {{sense|vomit}} [[kotzen]]

